FEAR 2 is a good game, with some cool gunfights and a passable story.
(+) Good pace, and OK gunplay;
(+) Great atmosphere;
(+) Nice controls;
(+) Cool guns;
(+) Good graphics and excellent performance;
(-) It can't hide the fact that it's 100% linear;
(-) Not enough memorable moments;
(-) Shotguns are a total letdown;
(-) I hate PDAs. Please, cut the PDAs and tell the story details through dialogue and interactive events.
(-) I'm not a huge fan of its horror elements which, IMO, leaves a lot to be desired, specially compared to games like Condemned, Undying and Penumbra, to name a few;
All in all, despite its many flaws, it's still way better than its predecessor and well worth the purchase.

